WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.997
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:03.998 --> 00:00:05.940
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:05.941 --> 00:00:07.207
The family business.

00:00:08.331 --> 00:00:10.411
Before dad died, he told me something.

00:00:10.481 --> 00:00:12.416
Something about you.
What's did he tell you?

00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:13.981
He said that I might
have to kill you, Sam.

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:15.407
What the hell is that supposed to mean?

00:00:15.408 --> 00:00:16.177
I don't know.

00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:17.580
Did he know the demon's plans for me?

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.391
Am I supposed to go
dark side or something?

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:20.993
Who are you? Please.

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:22.958
You're in danger.

00:00:22.984 --> 00:00:24.498
What's your name? Ava Wilson.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:26.754
You must be one of us. One of who?

00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:28.577
One of the psychics like me.

00:00:28.674 --> 00:00:30.432
There are others like us out there,

00:00:30.439 --> 00:00:32.236
And we're all part of something.

00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:34.070
I'm not part of anything, okay?

00:00:34.074 --> 00:00:34.792
Do you see this?

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:37.196
I am getting married in eight weeks.

00:00:37.231 --> 00:00:38.669
You can't run from this,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.232
And you can't protect me.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.116
I can try.

00:00:44.203 --> 00:00:46.191
Maybe I can help.
You've done all you can.

00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:48.925
Just go back to your
fianc. You'll be safe there.

00:00:48.953 --> 00:00:50.741
Promise me you'll call, then.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.091
I promise.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:53.907
Ava...

00:01:17.715 --> 00:01:19.272
Most of the stuff is up here.

00:01:19.315 --> 00:01:21.405
Still can't believe
you're closing this house.

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:23.337
My parents got engaged here.

00:01:23.844 --> 00:01:25.341
My grandparents too.

00:01:25.448 --> 00:01:27.345
Yeah, a lot of people did.

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:30.280
Boxes are at the end of
the hall. Need any help?

00:01:30.348 --> 00:01:31.673
No, ma'am. I got it.

00:01:38.232 --> 00:01:40.349
He's gonna take our toys?

00:01:40.807 --> 00:01:42.793
Only the ones you
don't play with anymore.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.341
It's not like you don't
have enough already.

00:01:46.244 --> 00:01:48.576
Son of a bitch. Son of a bitch.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.986
Watch your mouth.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.490
Maggie said it first.

00:01:51.575 --> 00:01:53.023
Watch your mouth too, Maggie.

00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:32.667
Good night, Tabitha.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.226
Oh my god! Yes, yes are you there?

00:03:06.232 --> 00:03:08.431
Please you have to send someone now.

00:03:09.477 --> 00:03:10.606
There's been an accident.

00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:13.652
A man fell down my stairs,
and I don't know if he's...

00:03:13.687 --> 00:03:16.226
His head is like
completely turned around.

00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:19.850
Tyler, don't look! Don't look!

00:03:20.327 --> 00:03:21.285
Oh yes, yes!

00:03:21.962 --> 00:03:23.529
As soon as possible.

00:03:27.329 --> 00:03:29.611
Just hurry, please hurry!

00:03:29.926 --> 00:03:32.576
I don't know, I didn't
see how it happened.

00:03:47.176 --> 00:03:48.384
Yeah.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.251
Okay. Thanks, Ellen.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:03:55.296
What did she have to
say? She got nothing.

00:03:55.762 --> 00:03:57.912
Me, I've been checking every
database I can think of,

00:03:57.978 --> 00:03:59.476
Federal, state, and local.

00:03:59.559 --> 00:04:01.798
No one's heard anything
about Ava. She's just...

00:04:01.843 --> 00:04:03.540
Into thin air, you know?

00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:05.585
What about you?

00:04:05.672 --> 00:04:08.340
No, same as before. Sorry, man.

00:04:09.586 --> 00:04:11.347
Ellen did have one thing.

00:04:12.124 --> 00:04:14.452
A hotel in Cornwall, Connecticut,

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:16.627
Two freak accidents in
the past three weeks.

00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:18.349
Yeah, what's that have to do with Ava?

00:04:18.755 --> 00:04:20.022
It's a job.

00:04:20.027 --> 00:04:21.934
I mean, a lady drowned in the bathtub,

00:04:21.971 --> 00:04:24.121
Then a few days ago, a
guy falls down the stairs,

00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:25.671
Head turns a complete 180,

00:04:25.677 --> 00:04:27.645
Which isn't exactly normal, you know?

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.650
Look, I don't know,
Dean, it might be nothing,

00:04:29.654 --> 00:04:31.875
But I told Ellen we'd
think about checking it out.

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:33.847
You did? Yeah.

00:04:36.266 --> 00:04:38.685
You seem surprised. Yeah,
it's just, you know...

00:04:39.113 --> 00:04:42.193
Not the patented Sam
Winchester way, is it?

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.124
What way is that?

00:04:44.202 --> 00:04:47.083
Just figured after Ava,
there'd be, you know, more

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:51.641
Angst and droopy music and
staring out the rainy windows.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.257
I'll shut up now.

00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:56.528
Look,

00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:58.854
I'm the one who told
her to go back home.

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:01.607
Now her fianc's dead,

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:04.602
And some demon has taken
her off to god knows where,

00:05:04.617 --> 00:05:05.897
You know?

00:05:07.164 --> 00:05:08.891
We've been looking for a month now,

00:05:09.538 --> 00:05:11.004
And we got nothing.

00:05:12.431 --> 00:05:14.142
So I'm not giving up on her, but

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.306
I'm not gonna let
other people die either.

00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:19.893
We got to save as many people as we can.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:25.260
Wow, that attitude is just
way too healthy for me.

00:05:25.705 --> 00:05:28.007
I'm officially
uncomfortable now. Thank you.

00:05:31.168 --> 00:05:33.105
All right, call Ellen.
Tell her we'll take it.

00:05:47.216 --> 00:05:49.263
Dude, this is sweet.

00:05:49.679 --> 00:05:51.841
I never get to work jobs like this.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.642
Like what?

00:05:54.149 --> 00:05:56.538
Old-School haunted houses. You know,

00:05:56.925 --> 00:05:59.673
Fog, secret passage ways,

00:05:59.678 --> 00:06:01.749
Sissy  british accents.

00:06:02.423 --> 00:06:05.074
Might even run into Fred and
Daphne while we're inside.

00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:09.372
Daphne... Love her.

00:06:12.854 --> 00:06:14.252
Hey, wait a sec.

00:06:15.659 --> 00:06:18.089
I'm not so sure haunted's the problem.

00:06:18.183 --> 00:06:19.269
What do you mean?

00:06:20.195 --> 00:06:21.515
You see this pattern here?

00:06:22.399 --> 00:06:25.199
That's a quincunx. It's a five-Spot.

00:06:25.847 --> 00:06:27.654
Five-Spot. Yeah.

00:06:27.678 --> 00:06:29.157
That's for hoodoo spellwork, isn't it?

00:06:29.163 --> 00:06:30.830
Right. Hey, you fill
this thing with bloodweed,

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.944
You got a powerful charm
to ward off enemies.

00:06:33.011 --> 00:06:34.647
Except I don't see any bloodweed.

00:06:34.774 --> 00:06:36.733
Don't you think this
place is a little too

00:06:37.299 --> 00:06:38.874
White-Meat for hoodoo?

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:41.891
Maybe.

00:06:47.827 --> 00:06:48.975
May I help you?

00:06:49.058 --> 00:06:51.951
Hi. Yeah, I'd like a room
for a couple of nights.

00:06:53.228 --> 00:06:54.105
Hey!

00:06:54.848 --> 00:06:57.258
Sorry about that. No problem.

00:06:57.343 --> 00:07:00.896
Well, congratulations. You could
be some of our final guests.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.300
Well, sounds vaguely ominous.

00:07:03.336 --> 00:07:06.154
No, I'm sorry. I mean, we're
closing at the end of the month.

00:07:07.174 --> 00:07:09.671
Let me guess. You guys
are here antiquing?

00:07:11.378 --> 00:07:14.000
How'd you know? You just look the type.

00:07:14.086 --> 00:07:15.873
So, a king-Size bed?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.238
What? No. No, no.

00:07:19.376 --> 00:07:21.973
Two singles. We're just brothers.

00:07:22.409 --> 00:07:25.332
Oh. Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:07:27.918 --> 00:07:29.867
What did you mean that
we looked the type?

00:07:31.665 --> 00:07:32.645
You know,

00:07:32.659 --> 00:07:35.567
Speaking of antiques, you have a really

00:07:35.573 --> 00:07:37.543
Interesting urn on the front porch.

00:07:37.608 --> 00:07:39.507
Where did you get that?
You know, I have no idea.

00:07:39.512 --> 00:07:40.637
It's been there forever.

00:07:40.982 --> 00:07:42.981
Here you go, Mr. Mahogoff.

00:07:44.268 --> 00:07:46.560
You'll be staying in room 237.

00:07:47.427 --> 00:07:49.754
Sherwin, could you show these
gentlemen to their rooms?

00:07:50.954 --> 00:07:52.061
Let me guess...

00:07:52.564 --> 00:07:53.931
Antiquers?

00:07:56.241 --> 00:07:57.928
I can give you a hand with that bag.

00:07:57.933 --> 00:07:59.481
I got it. Okay.

00:08:00.399 --> 00:08:01.996
So the hotel's closing up, huh?

00:08:01.996 --> 00:08:04.660
Yep. Miss Susan tried
to make a go of it,

00:08:04.743 --> 00:08:06.796
But the guests just don't
come like they used to.

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:09.327
Still, it's a damn shame. Oh yeah?

00:08:09.358 --> 00:08:13.119
It may not look it anymore,
but this place was a palace.

00:08:13.182 --> 00:08:16.244
Two different vice-Presidents
laid their heads on our pillows.

00:08:16.508 --> 00:08:19.920
My parents worked here. I
practically grew up here.

00:08:20.376 --> 00:08:21.682
I'm gonna miss it.

00:08:22.551 --> 00:08:23.778
Here's your room.

00:08:29.885 --> 00:08:30.821
Thanks.

00:08:38.561 --> 00:08:41.148
You're not gonna cheap
out on me, are you, boy?

00:08:50.349 --> 00:08:51.566
What the...

00:08:52.544 --> 00:08:53.591
What?

00:08:54.297 --> 00:08:55.517
That's normal.

00:08:56.593 --> 00:08:58.449
Why the hell would anyone stay here?

00:08:58.456 --> 00:09:00.383
I'm amazed they kept
in business this long.

00:09:01.852 --> 00:09:05.435
All right, victim number one,
Joan Edison, 43 years old,

00:09:05.467 --> 00:09:07.927
A realtor handling
the sale of the hotel.

00:09:07.971 --> 00:09:11.114
And victim number two
was Larry Williams,

00:09:11.118 --> 00:09:12.935
Moving some stuff out to goodwill.

00:09:13.001 --> 00:09:15.102
Well, there's a connexion. They're
both tied up in shutting the place down.

00:09:15.164 --> 00:09:17.113
Yeah, maybe someone here
doesn't want to leave,

00:09:17.118 --> 00:09:18.747
And they're using hoodoo to fight back.

00:09:18.842 --> 00:09:20.850
Who do you think our witch
doctor is. This Susan lady?

00:09:20.956 --> 00:09:22.165
Doesn't seem likely.

00:09:22.237 --> 00:09:23.848
I mean, she's the one selling.

00:09:23.921 --> 00:09:25.271
So, what then, Sherwin?

00:09:26.779 --> 00:09:28.135
I don't know.

00:09:29.083 --> 00:09:30.799
Of course, the most
troubling question is,

00:09:30.805 --> 00:09:32.531
Why do these people assume we're gay?

00:09:32.596 --> 00:09:33.936
You are kind of butch.

00:09:34.319 --> 00:09:36.258
Probably think you're over compensating.

00:09:37.796 --> 00:09:38.943
Right.

00:09:54.997 --> 00:09:55.886
Hey.

00:09:57.633 --> 00:10:00.023
Look at that. More hoodoo.

00:10:13.142 --> 00:10:14.738
Hi, there. Hi.

00:10:14.756 --> 00:10:16.104
Everything  okay with your room?

00:10:16.166 --> 00:10:17.455
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:19.216
Yeah, everything's great. Good.

00:10:23.211 --> 00:10:26.092
Well, I was just in the
middle of packing. So...

00:10:26.166 --> 00:10:29.557
Hey, are those antique dolls?

00:10:30.131 --> 00:10:31.953
'Cause this one, this one here,

00:10:31.958 --> 00:10:34.107
He's got a major doll
collection back home.

00:10:34.111 --> 00:10:35.619
Don't you? Huh?

00:10:38.789 --> 00:10:41.137
Big time. Big time.

00:10:41.234 --> 00:10:43.985
You think he could come in, well,
we could come in and take a look?

00:10:44.438 --> 00:10:47.129
I don't know. Please?
I mean, he loves them.

00:10:47.225 --> 00:10:48.189
He's not gonna tell you this,

00:10:48.196 --> 00:10:50.353
But he's always dressing them
up in little tiny outfits.

00:10:50.368 --> 00:10:53.659
You'd make his day. She would. Huh? Huh?

00:10:55.178 --> 00:10:56.325
It's true.

00:10:57.854 --> 00:10:59.881
Okay. Come on in. All right.

00:11:00.156 --> 00:11:01.063
All right!

00:11:06.317 --> 00:11:07.778
Wow.

00:11:08.764 --> 00:11:10.702
This is a lot of dolls.

00:11:10.766 --> 00:11:14.447
They're nice, you know.
They're not supercreepy at all.

00:11:15.145 --> 00:11:17.766
I suppose they are a little creepy.

00:11:17.811 --> 00:11:19.457
But they've been in the family forever.

00:11:19.475 --> 00:11:21.833
A lot of sentimental
value. What is this?

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.088
The hotel? Yeah, that's right.

00:11:24.113 --> 00:11:25.670
Exact replica, custom-Built.

00:11:33.849 --> 00:11:35.466
His head got twisted around.

00:11:37.605 --> 00:11:38.983
What happened to it?

00:11:39.048 --> 00:11:40.477
Tyler, probably.

00:11:40.552 --> 00:11:41.790
Mommy.

00:11:42.977 --> 00:11:44.706
Maggie's being mean.

00:11:44.799 --> 00:11:47.140
Tyler, tell her I said to be nice, okay?

00:11:47.212 --> 00:11:50.483
Hey, Tyler. I see you broke
your doll. You want me to fix it?

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.830
I didn't break it. I found it like that.

00:11:54.316 --> 00:11:58.220
Well, maybe Maggie did it.
No, neither of us did it.

00:11:58.233 --> 00:12:00.104
Grandma would get mad if we broke him.

00:12:00.197 --> 00:12:02.325
Tyler, she wouldn't get mad. Grandma?

00:12:03.513 --> 00:12:05.921
Grandma Rose. These were all her toys.

00:12:06.437 --> 00:12:07.807
Oh, really?

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.870
Where's grandma Rose now?

00:12:10.105 --> 00:12:11.543
Up in her room.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.969
You know, I'd really
love to talk to Rose

00:12:14.974 --> 00:12:16.782
About her incredible doll... No.

00:12:19.452 --> 00:12:20.638
I  mean,

00:12:21.044 --> 00:12:22.473
I'm  afraid that's impossible.

00:12:22.567 --> 00:12:26.169
My mother's been very sick, and
she's not taking any visitors.

00:12:31.504 --> 00:12:33.031
What do you think?

00:12:33.119 --> 00:12:34.544
Dolls, hoodoo,

00:12:34.549 --> 00:12:36.527
Mysterious shut-In grandma?

00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:39.977
Well, dolls are used in all
kind of voodoo and hoodoo,

00:12:40.011 --> 00:12:42.750
Like curses and binding spells.

00:12:42.784 --> 00:12:44.822
Yeah, maybe we found our witch doctor.

00:12:44.918 --> 00:12:47.180
I'll go see what I can dig upon granny.

00:12:47.184 --> 00:12:49.815
You get online, check old obits,
freak accidents. That sort of things.

00:12:49.849 --> 00:12:51.875
See if she's whacked
anybody before. Right.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:54.420
Don't go surfing porn. It's
not the kind of whacking I mean.

00:12:59.966 --> 00:13:01.586
I've been meaning to ask...

00:13:01.589 --> 00:13:03.570
What sort of renovations
are you planning?

00:13:03.645 --> 00:13:04.939
They never told you?

00:13:04.947 --> 00:13:06.444
Told me what?

00:13:06.537 --> 00:13:09.380
Miss Thompson, we plan
on demolishing the hotel.

00:13:10.377 --> 00:13:12.653
Oh. I see.

00:13:13.914 --> 00:13:15.220
Excuse me.

00:14:41.111 --> 00:14:42.187
What happened?

00:14:42.875 --> 00:14:46.667
The maid went into turn down
the sheets, and he was just

00:14:47.152 --> 00:14:49.372
Hanging there. That's awful.

00:14:49.378 --> 00:14:50.695
He was a guest?

00:14:50.738 --> 00:14:52.656
He worked for the company
that bought the place.

00:14:55.117 --> 00:14:57.607
I don't understand. What?

00:14:57.631 --> 00:15:00.102
Had a lot of bad luck around here.

00:15:01.136 --> 00:15:04.080
Look, if you'd like to check
out, I'll give you a full refund.

00:15:04.102 --> 00:15:06.655
No, thanks. I don't scare that easy.

00:15:15.204 --> 00:15:16.583
There's been another one.

00:15:16.586 --> 00:15:18.386
Some guy just hung himself in his room.

00:15:19.039 --> 00:15:21.219
Yeah. I saw.

00:15:21.284 --> 00:15:22.823
We got figure this out and fast.

00:15:23.178 --> 00:15:24.717
What did you find out about granny?

00:15:26.453 --> 00:15:27.880
You're bossy.

00:15:29.699 --> 00:15:30.608
What?

00:15:31.834 --> 00:15:33.461
You're bossy.

00:15:34.689 --> 00:15:35.887
You're short.

00:15:37.083 --> 00:15:39.043
Are you drunk? Yeah.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:40.914
So?

00:15:41.232 --> 00:15:42.438
Stupid.

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:46.237
Dude, what are you thinking?
We're working a case.

00:15:49.837 --> 00:15:52.818
That guy who hung himself...

00:15:55.157 --> 00:15:57.047
I couldn't save him. What
are you talking about?

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.319
You didn't know. You
couldn't have done anything.

00:15:58.322 --> 00:15:59.949
That's an excuse, Dean.

00:16:01.409 --> 00:16:03.707
I should have found a way to save him.

00:16:05.266 --> 00:16:07.254
I should have saved Ava too.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.109
Well, you can't save
everyone. Even you said that.

00:16:10.204 --> 00:16:12.231
No, Dean, you don't
understand, all right?

00:16:12.246 --> 00:16:14.906
The more people I save,
the more I can change.

00:16:14.982 --> 00:16:17.523
Change what? My destiny, Dean.

00:16:20.092 --> 00:16:22.310
All right, time for
bed. Come on, sasquatch.

00:16:22.315 --> 00:16:23.333
Come on.

00:16:23.418 --> 00:16:25.976
I need you to watch out
for me. Yeah, I always do.

00:16:26.073 --> 00:16:29.102
No. No, no, no. You have
to watch out for me...

00:16:29.871 --> 00:16:31.247
All right?

00:16:31.782 --> 00:16:34.985
And if I ever turn into
something that I'm not...

00:16:37.853 --> 00:16:39.793
You have to kill me. Sam...

00:16:39.827 --> 00:16:42.257
Dean, dad told you
to do it. You have to.

00:16:43.023 --> 00:16:44.853
Yeah, well, dad's an ass.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.227
He never should have said
anything. I mean, you don't do that.

00:16:47.242 --> 00:16:49.069
You don't lay that
kinda crap on your kids.

00:16:49.134 --> 00:16:51.214
No, he was right to say it.

00:16:51.722 --> 00:16:53.899
Who knows what I might become?

00:16:53.983 --> 00:16:56.485
Even now, everyone around me dies.

00:16:56.577 --> 00:16:58.967
Well, I'm not dying, okay?

00:16:59.055 --> 00:17:00.653
And neither are you. Come on, sit down.

00:17:00.927 --> 00:17:04.458
No, please, Dean, you're
the only one who can do it.

00:17:04.853 --> 00:17:06.554
Promise me. Don't ask that of me.

00:17:06.629 --> 00:17:07.886
Dean, please.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.776
You have to promise me.

00:17:15.693 --> 00:17:17.050
I promise.

00:17:20.242 --> 00:17:21.579
Thanks.

00:17:24.378 --> 00:17:25.826
Thank you...

00:18:07.479 --> 00:18:09.047
Find any good antiques?

00:18:09.652 --> 00:18:12.785
No, no. Got distracted.

00:18:13.431 --> 00:18:14.497
Have a drink.

00:18:14.692 --> 00:18:16.311
Yeah, thanks.

00:18:20.493 --> 00:18:23.954
So, poor guy, huh, killing himself?

00:18:25.152 --> 00:18:28.123
That kind of thing seems
to be going around lately.

00:18:28.197 --> 00:18:30.684
Yeah. Yeah, I heard
about the other ones.

00:18:30.771 --> 00:18:34.313
It's almost like this hotel
is cursed or something.

00:18:34.316 --> 00:18:36.996
Every hotel has its spilled blood.

00:18:38.567 --> 00:18:40.193
If people only knew what's going on

00:18:40.198 --> 00:18:42.376
In some of those rooms
they've checked into.

00:18:44.465 --> 00:18:46.343
You know a lot about
the place, don't you?

00:18:46.371 --> 00:18:48.159
Down to the last nail.

00:18:48.935 --> 00:18:50.784
I'd love to hear some stories.

00:18:51.678 --> 00:18:52.938
Boy,

00:18:53.344 --> 00:18:55.890
You should never say that to an old man.

00:19:00.084 --> 00:19:03.265
This is little miss Susan
and her mother, Rose.

00:19:03.632 --> 00:19:05.147
Happier days.

00:19:08.601 --> 00:19:10.247
They're not happy now?

00:19:10.625 --> 00:19:14.236
Well, would you be, leaving
the only home you ever knew?

00:19:15.101 --> 00:19:16.831
I don't know. I never really knew one.

00:19:16.855 --> 00:19:18.853
Well, this is Rose's home.

00:19:18.859 --> 00:19:20.958
Been in the family over a century.

00:19:21.032 --> 00:19:23.130
Used to be the family estate,

00:19:23.138 --> 00:19:26.730
And now she gets to live in
some senior-Living graveyard,

00:19:26.765 --> 00:19:28.833
And they tear this place down.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:31.525
That's too bad.

00:19:33.104 --> 00:19:35.446
I hear Rose isn't feeling well either.

00:19:35.451 --> 00:19:36.625
No, she isn't.

00:19:37.173 --> 00:19:38.271
What's wrong with her?

00:19:38.634 --> 00:19:40.624
It's not my business to say.

00:19:45.767 --> 00:19:47.404
Who's this?

00:19:48.173 --> 00:19:49.920
That's Rose

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:52.527
When she was a little girl.

00:20:00.174 --> 00:20:01.751
Who's that with her?

00:20:01.859 --> 00:20:03.575
That's her nanny, Marie.

00:20:03.579 --> 00:20:06.231
She looked after Rose
more than her own mother.

00:20:29.067 --> 00:20:30.696
How you feeling, Sammy?

00:20:32.272 --> 00:20:36.063
I guess mixing whiskey and jager
wasn't such a gangbuster idea, was it?

00:20:38.644 --> 00:20:41.313
I'll bet you don't remember a
thing from last night, do you?

00:20:41.318 --> 00:20:43.600
No, I can still taste the tequila.

00:20:45.306 --> 00:20:47.766
You know, there's a really
good hangover remedy. It's uh...

00:20:47.852 --> 00:20:51.463
It's a greasy pork sandwich
served up in a dirty ashtray.

00:20:51.509 --> 00:20:53.365
Oh, I hate you. I know you do.

00:20:54.775 --> 00:20:57.155
Hey, turns out when
grandma Rose was a tyke,

00:20:57.808 --> 00:21:01.112
She had a creole nanny
who wore a hoodoo necklace.

00:21:02.759 --> 00:21:05.318
So you think she taught
Rose hoodoo? Yes, I do.

00:21:07.587 --> 00:21:08.623
All right.

00:21:10.803 --> 00:21:12.971
I think it's time we talk to Rose, then.

00:21:13.076 --> 00:21:15.026
Oh, you need to brush your teeth first.

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:26.368
Hello?

00:21:27.765 --> 00:21:29.142
Susan?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:31.928
Clear?

00:22:57.049 --> 00:22:58.607
Mrs. Thompson?

00:23:02.245 --> 00:23:03.937
Mrs. Thompson?

00:23:06.976 --> 00:23:08.202
Rose?

00:23:11.395 --> 00:23:14.735
Hi, Mrs. Thompson. We're not
here to hurt you. It's okay. We...

00:23:18.678 --> 00:23:20.005
Rose?

00:23:25.539 --> 00:23:26.296
Dean.

00:23:30.058 --> 00:23:31.834
This woman's had a stroke.

00:23:33.114 --> 00:23:35.113
Yeah, but hoodoo's hands-On. Yeah.

00:23:35.117 --> 00:23:37.736
You got to mix herbs and
chant, build an altar.

00:23:38.041 --> 00:23:39.652
So it can't be Rose.

00:23:39.687 --> 00:23:42.555
Hey, maybe it's not even hoodoo.
You know, she could be faking.

00:23:42.590 --> 00:23:44.399
What do you want to do,
poke her with a stick?

00:23:45.607 --> 00:23:47.554
Dude, you're not gonna
poke her with a stick.

00:23:47.638 --> 00:23:48.997
What the hell?

00:23:49.044 --> 00:23:50.570
What are you doing in here?

00:23:50.896 --> 00:23:52.513
We just wanted to talk to Rose.

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:54.388
Look at her. She's
scared out of her wits.

00:23:54.484 --> 00:23:56.570
I want you out of my
hotel in two minutes

00:23:56.578 --> 00:23:57.822
Or I'm calling the cops.

00:24:14.969 --> 00:24:16.997
Your turn. Eightsies.

00:24:23.697 --> 00:24:25.334
Have you started packing yet?

00:24:25.348 --> 00:24:26.957
No. Why not?

00:24:27.032 --> 00:24:28.389
I don't want to move.

00:24:28.453 --> 00:24:30.914
Yes, I know, but we have to.

00:24:30.938 --> 00:24:33.017
But Maggie says we're
not allowed to move.

00:24:33.061 --> 00:24:33.910
Yeah?

00:24:34.547 --> 00:24:38.357
Tyler, enough. Maggie is imaginary.

00:24:38.404 --> 00:24:41.522
You're too old to have an imaginary
friend, and I am done pretending.

00:24:45.636 --> 00:24:47.285
I don't like her.

00:25:08.668 --> 00:25:10.538
I  could lug those boxes for you.

00:25:10.541 --> 00:25:12.429
I got it, Sherwin. Thanks.

00:25:12.453 --> 00:25:13.822
Okay, then.

00:25:14.300 --> 00:25:15.596
See you later.

00:27:21.021 --> 00:27:23.297
You okay? I think so.

00:27:24.245 --> 00:27:26.136
Come on. Come on. Let's
get inside. Let's go.

00:27:29.847 --> 00:27:32.205
Whiskey. Sure.

00:27:32.240 --> 00:27:33.727
I know the feeling.

00:27:35.417 --> 00:27:37.286
What the hell happened out there?

00:27:38.052 --> 00:27:39.760
You want the truth? Of course.

00:27:39.823 --> 00:27:42.032
At first, we thought it was
some sort of a hoodoo curse,

00:27:42.497 --> 00:27:43.725
But that out there...

00:27:44.162 --> 00:27:45.979
That was definitely a spirit.

00:27:46.537 --> 00:27:47.705
Here.

00:27:48.499 --> 00:27:50.028
You're insane.

00:27:50.844 --> 00:27:52.042
It's been said.

00:27:52.066 --> 00:27:53.233
Look, I'm sorry, Susan.

00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:55.379
We don't exactly have
time to ease you into this,

00:27:55.413 --> 00:27:57.641
But we need to know when
your mother had the stroke.

00:27:58.026 --> 00:28:00.707
What does that have to do...
Just answer the question.

00:28:01.494 --> 00:28:02.813
About a month ago.

00:28:03.026 --> 00:28:04.764
Right before the killings began.

00:28:04.769 --> 00:28:06.046
You see?

00:28:06.124 --> 00:28:09.605
So what if Rose was working hoodoo,
but not to hurt anyone, to protect them?

00:28:09.710 --> 00:28:11.969
She was using the urn patterns
to ward off the spirit.

00:28:12.032 --> 00:28:13.832
Right. Until she had a
stroke and couldn't anymore.

00:28:13.846 --> 00:28:15.253
I don't believe this. Listen,

00:28:15.288 --> 00:28:17.888
That car didn't try to run
you down by itself, okay?

00:28:18.746 --> 00:28:22.157
I mean, I guess it did technically,
but with a spirit. Forget it.

00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:23.309
Just believe what you want, alright?

00:28:23.362 --> 00:28:25.443
But the fact is you and
your family are in danger.

00:28:25.539 --> 00:28:27.526
So you need to clear
everybody out of here.

00:28:27.602 --> 00:28:28.937
Your employees,

00:28:28.943 --> 00:28:30.019
Your mother,

00:28:30.026 --> 00:28:31.754
Your daughters, everyone.

00:28:34.133 --> 00:28:37.364
I only have one daughter. One?

00:28:37.408 --> 00:28:39.099
I thought Tyler had
a sister named Maggie.

00:28:40.134 --> 00:28:41.851
Maggie's imaginary.

00:28:44.474 --> 00:28:45.549
Where's Tyler?

00:28:51.546 --> 00:28:53.915
She's going to stay here with me,

00:28:54.612 --> 00:28:56.590
And you can't stop me.

00:28:57.056 --> 00:29:00.278
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:29:02.667 --> 00:29:05.505
Maggie, don't. You're not
supposed to bother grandma.

00:29:06.223 --> 00:29:07.068
I know.

00:29:09.198 --> 00:29:10.435
Come on.

00:29:11.513 --> 00:29:12.988
Let's play.

00:29:13.507 --> 00:29:15.465
Can we have a tea party?

00:29:30.458 --> 00:29:31.605
Tyler!

00:29:35.896 --> 00:29:38.544
Oh, my god! Tyler!

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:44.448
She's not here!

00:29:46.795 --> 00:29:47.804
Susan,

00:29:48.230 --> 00:29:50.306
Tell us what you know
about Maggie. Not much.

00:29:50.384 --> 00:29:52.412
Tyler's been talking about
her since mom got sick.

00:29:52.456 --> 00:29:54.066
Okay, did you ever know
anyone by that name?

00:29:54.068 --> 00:29:55.387
Uh no. Think, think.

00:29:55.412 --> 00:29:57.600
Somebody that could have lived
here, might have passed away.

00:29:58.035 --> 00:30:00.708
My god... My mom had
a sister named Margaret.

00:30:00.743 --> 00:30:01.777
She barely spoke about her.

00:30:01.785 --> 00:30:03.670
Did Margaret die here
when she was a kid?

00:30:03.758 --> 00:30:05.547
Yeah, she drowned in the pool.

00:30:06.460 --> 00:30:07.389
Come on.

00:30:26.788 --> 00:30:28.519
I don't like it up here.

00:30:28.522 --> 00:30:30.260
I'm scared.

00:30:30.365 --> 00:30:31.962
It's okay.

00:30:31.968 --> 00:30:33.908
All you have to do is jump.

00:30:36.826 --> 00:30:38.587
I can't swim.

00:30:38.671 --> 00:30:39.777
I know.

00:30:40.303 --> 00:30:41.751
But it won't hurt.

00:30:41.777 --> 00:30:42.952
I promise.

00:30:43.027 --> 00:30:46.210
And then we can be together forever,

00:30:46.215 --> 00:30:48.573
And no one will bother us.

00:30:53.037 --> 00:30:55.528
Why don't you just
come with me and mommy?

00:30:55.603 --> 00:30:59.293
Because I can't leave here,
and you can't leave me.

00:31:02.937 --> 00:31:04.354
Please.

00:31:04.378 --> 00:31:06.064
I don't want to be alone.

00:31:19.945 --> 00:31:21.174
Tyler!

00:31:26.238 --> 00:31:27.444
Mommy!

00:31:33.713 --> 00:31:34.958
Is there another entrance?

00:31:35.012 --> 00:31:36.660
Around back. All right, let's go!

00:31:36.716 --> 00:31:37.635
Keep working.

00:32:02.532 --> 00:32:04.621
It'll all be over soon.

00:32:06.533 --> 00:32:07.489
Stand back.

00:32:10.507 --> 00:32:12.118
Son of a bitch.

00:32:19.005 --> 00:32:20.530
Margaret...

00:32:23.060 --> 00:32:25.121
Margaret...

00:33:28.963 --> 00:33:30.459
Oh, thank god. Thank god!

00:33:30.907 --> 00:33:32.011
Mommy?

00:33:32.076 --> 00:33:33.547
Yeah, baby, I'm here.

00:33:34.181 --> 00:33:36.732
Tyler, do you see Maggie anywhere?

00:33:38.237 --> 00:33:39.755
No, she's gone.

00:33:52.704 --> 00:33:54.554
You'd really do that for me?

00:34:01.230 --> 00:34:02.659
Yes...

00:34:02.733 --> 00:34:04.181
If you did,

00:34:04.687 --> 00:34:06.223
I'd let them go.

00:34:08.456 --> 00:34:10.333
But I don't understand.

00:34:10.376 --> 00:34:13.249
You kept me away for so long.

00:34:14.034 --> 00:34:16.602
I thought you didn't love me anymore.

00:34:21.177 --> 00:34:22.413
Okay...

00:34:23.039 --> 00:34:24.497
Little sister.

00:34:39.450 --> 00:34:41.217
Don't worry, honey. We're
leaving in two minutes.

00:34:41.315 --> 00:34:42.450
We just got to get grandma.

00:34:45.731 --> 00:34:47.412
I don't get it. Did Maggie just stop?

00:34:48.967 --> 00:34:51.258
Seems like it. Where
the hell did she go?

00:35:20.346 --> 00:35:22.354
Paramedics said it was another stroke.

00:35:23.390 --> 00:35:24.417
Do you think...

00:35:24.942 --> 00:35:27.224
Margaret could have had
something to do with it?

00:35:27.890 --> 00:35:28.967
We don't know.

00:35:29.063 --> 00:35:30.387
But it's possible,

00:35:30.395 --> 00:35:31.589
Yeah.

00:35:34.309 --> 00:35:35.938
Susan, I'm sorry.

00:35:36.476 --> 00:35:38.694
You have nothing to apologize for.

00:35:38.730 --> 00:35:41.017
You've given me everything.

00:35:43.887 --> 00:35:45.057
Ready to go, kiddo?

00:35:45.079 --> 00:35:46.328
Yeah.

00:35:46.954 --> 00:35:49.192
Tyler, you're sure
Maggie's not around anymore?

00:35:49.250 --> 00:35:51.155
I'm sure. I'd see her.

00:35:56.620 --> 00:35:58.961
I guess whatever's
going on must be over.

00:36:04.147 --> 00:36:06.275
You two take care of
yourselves, all right?

00:36:10.736 --> 00:36:12.064
Thank you.

00:36:12.601 --> 00:36:13.609
Yeah.

00:36:13.614 --> 00:36:14.991
Both of you.

00:36:24.471 --> 00:36:27.052
Think you could have hooked
up some milf action there, bud.

00:36:27.057 --> 00:36:29.015
Serious, I think she liked you. Yeah,

00:36:29.031 --> 00:36:30.568
That's all she needs.

00:36:30.654 --> 00:36:32.824
Well, you saved the
mommy, you saved the girl.

00:36:32.826 --> 00:36:34.124
Not a bad day.

00:36:34.230 --> 00:36:35.980
'Course,you know, I could
have saved them myself,

00:36:36.062 --> 00:36:37.731
But I didn't want you to feel useless.

00:36:38.159 --> 00:36:39.755
All right, I appreciate it.

00:36:40.480 --> 00:36:42.720
Feels good getting back
in the saddle, doesn't it?

00:36:44.009 --> 00:36:44.973
Yeah.

00:36:45.812 --> 00:36:47.188
Yeah, it does.

00:36:47.215 --> 00:36:49.913
But it doesn't change what we
talked about last night, Dean.

00:36:51.501 --> 00:36:53.482
We talked about a lot
of things last night.

00:36:54.336 --> 00:36:56.155
You know what I mean. You were wasted.

00:36:56.261 --> 00:36:57.146
But you weren't...

00:36:58.276 --> 00:36:59.791
And you promised.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.043
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
